You could try setting the SONAME when you build the shared object.  Normally,
this is set to the last (filename) component of the object.  For example
the SONAME of /some/where/libfoo.so is "libfoo.so".  You can hardcode a
path to a library by setting the SONAME to the full pathname of the library.

	ld -shared -soname /some/where/libfoo.so -o libfoo.so *.o ...

See the loader(5) man page for details.

						Frank


