I thought I finally had a decent idea about making memory read-only at
granularities other than page sizes, which would be really neat for
malloc debugging (cf. efence).

Here's the idea:

Have the memory managed by malloc be an mmapped file.  To make memory
read-only, have another process do mandatory record locking.

But it turns out that altering mmapped memory bypasses record locking.
(Another implementation doesn't even allow simultaneous mmapping and
record locking.)

Say it ain't so!  Or is there another way to solve this?

Chris


