I've noticed a misfeature in the DEC OSF/1 `ps' command:

If you use the `ps' command, the width of the output is automatically
truncated to the width of the terminal *even* if the output isn't
going to the terminal.

Thus, if you do `ps aux | grep cron' on an 80 column terminal it
won't find your `cron' process.

DEC, please consider turning this terminal width feature off when
the stdout isn't a tty.

Ray.
