My apologies for not providing enough information.

All C code has been compiled with "-g -std1 -shared" compile options.

All Fortran code has been compiled with "-g -c -col72 -cross_reference -K -v -V -std -names as_is -assume nounderscore -shared" compile options.

All shared libraries are build with ld using the -shared option, i.e.,
       ld -shared object.list library.name

All linking is done with either cc or f77 using the -call_shared option.  I am
using threads and the library search path does include the "-lpthreads -lmach
-lc_r" libraries.

I am using the LD_LIBRARY_PATH environmental variable in the form
/path/to to provide the location of the shared libraries I built.

