> More than normal; it is required behavior. A program can detach, then
> re-attach, and expect to find data still there.

But it defeats resource tracking. If you need to keep a segment in core
you can keep a dummy process around to hold it's hand. In the more common
case you *want* segments to go away when you're done with them.

It's not just more limited than mmap(), it's not in keeping with the UNIX
design philosophy.
