print job is delayed for some 10's of seconds of timeout(?) before
printing, and some PostScript jobs (apparently those lacking the explicit
EOF character the printer expects from PC hosts) never print, OR if the
queue is configured with an explicit EOF at the end of every job, the
printer ejects a blank page between every job, even if successive jobs are
the same type (i.e. PostScript right after PostScript or ASCII [PCL] after
ASCII).

    Since we print a mix of PostScript and ASCII files, this is a major
drag. Currently, while some users are printing out a large number of
single-page PostScript files (plots), I have reset the printer to expect
PostScript only, so ASCII jobs choke as PostScript errors. Clearly, this
is not a viable, long-term solution.

    Has anybody else on a unix platform for which HP does not supply
filters (meaning other than HP and Sun) come up with a solution to this
problem?

    BTW, naturally, the printing from the Macs works perfectly, since it
employs an HP-supplied driver.

