>Soooo.  What do i do to cork the memory leaks?  Here's the gruesome

Have you added -terminate to the line in /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers ?

According to the Release Notes this switch should be added to avoid
that the Xserver grows without bound (apparently it leaks 2.4 MB per
logout/login recycle.).

>I'm also getting process table full errors.  ps aux report s 273 processes
>running, which ain't all that much.  Is it related to the memory problem?
>and how do i increase the size of the table?

I don't have the manuals here, but a fast look at param.h makes it
clear that with 'maxusers 32' (the default) and without NPROC defined
it will support 276 (the formula used is 20+maxuser*8 or NPROC if it's
defined).

I would recommend that you change maxusers to 64 and creates a new
kernel. In addition to this you migh change NPROC, but without manuals
I can't tell you what you should put into the kernel configuration
file.


