reserves the right to accept or reject field test sites for any reason.

DEC Fortran 90
--------------
The new ANSI and ISO Fortran standard defines a larger, more feature-rich 
language and provides a more robust set of language features that translate 
into productivity improvements for the scientific community.  In the United 
States, the Fortran 90 standard and the older Fortran 77 standard coexist, 
while in Europe, Fortran 90 is the only standard.

A new definition for the development of parallel Fortran applications has
been proposed by the High Performance Fortran Forum (HPFF) and referred to
as the High Performance Fortran Specification.  The HPF Forum, started in
part as a result of proposals by Digital, is a consortium of vendors, users,
research laboratories, and universities that set out to create an
industry-consensus on a small set of extensions to the new Fortran 90
standard, called the HPF extensions.

Digital's response to both the new Fortran 90 standard and the HPF
extensions is a product called DEC Fortran 90, and is the newest member of
the DEC Fortran family of COHESION compilers.  The DEC Fortran 90 language
is fully compliant with the ANSI and ISO Fortran 90 standards and supports a
subset of the de facto standard High Performance Fortran (HPF) Language
Specification. 

Digital Parallel Software Environment
-------------------------------------
Digital developed the Digital Parallel Software Environment to allow for
execution and debugging of parallel DEC Fortran 90 applications on Alpha AXP
systems running the DEC OSF/1 AXP operating system, Digital's implementation of
UNIX.  This software contains a parallel profiler and the system software,
which consists of an execution environment and several utilities.  The
Digital Parallel Software Environment, in combination with the DEC Fortran
90 compiler, allows programmers to quickly develop parallel programs on a
single workstation, then recompile and execute on Alpha AXP systems running
in parallel and/or running in multiprocessor configurations.  Together, DEC
Fortran 90 and the Digital Parallel Software Environment are commonly
referred to as "Digital High Performance Fortran 90".

