It looks to me that your program was compiled to use a shared library
which is now can't find.  If you have librca.so outside of the default
search path for loader, which is: /usr/shlib, /usr/ccs/lib,
/usr/lib/cmplrs/cc, /usr/lib, /usr/local/lib, /var/shlib.  

To modify the search path, you can do:

	setenv LD_LIBRARY_PATH "/path/to/librca.so

or you can try this when compiling your code:

	ld -rpath "/path/to/librca.so" main.o -o main -L/path/to" -lrca

I haven't tested this myself, but that's how I read the man page for
loader.


