In article <2vsfib$s9l@news.service.uci.edu> iglesias@draco.acs.uci.edu (Mike Iglesias) writes:
>You can get the changes to make a kernel from:
>        ftp://ftp.adelaide.edu.au/pub/av/multicast/ipmulti-decosf1.tar.Z
>
>Since they are not official patches, you're on your own if you have
>problems with them.  I've been using them since November or so with
>no problems.

Just to make things fully clear: these were never meant as patches
for people to use widely.  These bits were given to a few helpful
customers to help the DEC engineers test their multicast code, and
nobody ever expected them to work completely.  I strongly recommend
that anyone wanting to use IP multicast instead upgrade to OSF V2.0
(or later), in which the multicast code is officially supported.

Several versions of the V1.3 multicast code got out, some of which
had a different API than the V2.0 version.  So if you use these
V1.3 bits, don't be surprised if you have compatibility bugs.

-Jeff


