In article <2ve9cu$m4u@cisun2000.unil.ch>, khofmann@isrec-sun1.unil.ch (Kay Hofmann) writes:
>
>is there any simple possibility to log the traffic on an anonymous FTP
>server running under OSF1 2.0?
>
>I have found in the documentation how to monitor all actions of the ftpd,
>but I don't get ever this to work. I would be more interested, if only
>anonymous FTP would be logged.
>
Kay;

  In /etc/inetd.conf, change the line:

ftp     stream  tcp     nowait  root  /usr/sbin/ftpd          ftpd

  to:

ftp     stream  tcp     nowait  root  /usr/sbin/ftpd          ftpd -l

  This will cause the ftpd daemon to log to:

	/var/adm/syslog.dated/**DATE**/daemon.log

  There are also other freely-available ftp-daemons (ftpd-wu, for instance)
which support additional log and message options. Try gatekeeper.dec.com
or sunsite.unc.edu for starters. 

Craig
