[...]
>If I do a MAKEDEV rmt1x (where x is a - g ) it tells me device unknown.
>
>What would be the proper device to make for this dat drive?

First off, the device base name should be "tz".  This should be
followed by a number.  The number is the SCSI bus number (the
first one being number 0) times eight plus the SCSI ID of the 
device.  For example, for a tape device SCSI ID 3 on the 5th 
SCSI bus you would do "MAKEDEV tz35".

