A while ago I read the source code and found that passwd reads from
/dev/tty which is the controlling tty of the current process, rather
than stdin.

In order to do what you want, I ran the change script with "at" which
is started by the init process and thus has no controlling tty.  It
then defaults to read stdin.  This was all done on a Sun with SUNOS4.X
so I don't know how similar the source code to passwd is in OSF/1.
