>Does OSF running on an ALPHA server support diskless ALPHA OSF client
>workstations?  I.e. does OSF require every ALPHA workstation to have a
>local system disk?  If diskless operation is allowed which version of OSF
>did it start with?
>
>Don Summers
>summers@fnalv.fnal.gov

DEC OSF/1 does not currently support diskless operation, and indeed each
system needs to have a local disk for the O/S. The next major release
I believe will support dataless clients (i.e. swap on local disk, O/S
on remote server) and some future major release may support diskless.

