Do a `stty`.  If you see "speed 0 baud" in the first line, type `stty 9600`.

Or, as part of a C program:

        #include <sys/ioctl.h>
        struct  sgttyb sgttyb;
        (void)ioctl(0, TIOCGETP, &sgttyb);
        sgttyb.sg_flags |= B9600;
        (void)ioctl(0, TIOCSETP, &sgttyb);


It is a bug somewhere, but I don't know enough about OSF/1 internals to
guess where.  I just know that the above solution solves a lot of problems,
including the ones you've mentioned.


Peter



