gettimeofday() is indicated as obsolete, and that you should use getclock()
(which is indicated as "Trial Usage")!

At least in V2.0 Rev. 240 and before, the constant TIMEOFDAY which you
are supposed to give it is not correctly defined in the header files. Had
to do with either having or not having some POSIX symbol defined already.
It ought to work as advertised without doing anything special or using
any special compiler flags.

Other than that, getclock() works fine for me. Be sure you are using the
correct structure for the return, as there are about 8 different, incompatible
time structures for the 10 or so different methods of doing timers, getting
process times and time of day/elapsed time/date-and-time/etc.


