In article <300vfh$g85@hopper.acm.org>, daveotto@ACM.ORG (Dave Otto daveotto@acm.org) writes:

>Does anyone have a disktab entry for a seagate ST12550N drive?  Currently
>running 1.3, planning the 2.0 upgrade.  We would like to install the drive
>before the upgrade.

You may not really need one.  For well behaved disks, the disklabel
command can query the driver for the default partition table and
disk geometry (DEVGETGEOM).  Just specifiy the disk name on the
disklabel command and if it can't find a disktab entry it should
handle it.  Example:

	# disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c st12550n

Once labeled you can repartition to taste.  Newfs will use the
label information when it is present to get what it needs about
the geometry, partitioning and default block and fragment size.

