>In the prom monitor the dat drive shows up fine with a show device.
>If I do a MAKEDEV rmt1x (where x is a - g ) it tells me device unknown.
>What would be the proper device to make for this dat drive?

SCSI tape drives have names of the form "tz#", where # is usually
(bus * 8 + target).  For typical configuration the bus number would
be either 0 (internal bus) or 1 (external bus).  The target number
is the SCSI ID number assigned to the device.  So, a tape on the
internal SCSI at target 1 would be "tz1".  A device on the external
bus, target 1 would be "tz9" (1 * 8 + 1).  The particular console
may be smart enough to guess at the likely name and include that
next to the VMS device name.

When MAKEDEV creates the tape files they will be:

	rmt#{l,a,m,h}
	nrmt#{l,a,m,h}

Where # in this case is assigned sequentially depending on what
other tape devices exist.  The first tape will be rmt0, the 2nd
rmt1 and so on.  The trailing letters are used used to designate
the different densities; l = low, h = high, a and m = medium.
This naming convention is explained in the mtio(7) manual page.

