with GCC 2.5.8.

>  It's mainly the db package support than needs doing
>from memory.  I know someone was working on it...

The db package is not part of the sendmail distribution.  It is part of
4.4BSD.  Sendmail has certain optional features that rely on it, but
you can build a fine sendmail binary without the UCB libdb.  However, I
do believe that v1.79 of the db package does work on the Alpha.  I am
not using it currently myself (at least not on the Alphas).

