    This problem had been previously encountered by the Dec Fortran and I
    believe a dbx correction is in the works.

    In the meantime here's an example workaround.

gemosf.zko.dec.com> f77 main1.f -o main1
gemosf.zko.dec.com> f77 main2.f -o main2
gemosf.zko.dec.com> dbx main1
dbx version 3.11.4
Type 'help' for help.

main:    Source not available
(dbx) q
gemosf.zko.dec.com> dbx main2
dbx version 3.11.4
Type 'help' for help.

maine:   2  end
(dbx) q
gemosf.zko.dec.com> more main1.f
       program main
       end
gemosf.zko.dec.com> more main2.f
       program maine
       end
gemosf.zko.dec.com>

    That is, dbx seems to lose track of the program name main, substituting
    the program name allows proper lookup.

							Dennis


