This is almost always due to a heap corruption caused by the
application writing where is should not be writing, and almost
always then with at array overrun (past the end of the array).

A helpful tool for chasing heap corruptions can be found
via anonymous ftp from gatekeeper.dec.com:/pub/misc/malloc_dbg/*
Be sure to read the file ./contrib/dec_notes in the tar file, 
and hide gcc while building the library (at least I had many,
many problems using gcc building the library).

/Dave

