I found that some of the pbm filters on our copy of the freeware CD-ROM are
broken.  Several programs and functions within pbm assume that longs are
32 bits.  If I remember right, there was also a problem with the xwd filters
because the color map structure on the Alphas appears to be padded to a
quadword boundary.  Things that read and write the entries one at a time
work, but things that try to do a bunch of them at once by assuming the
total size is n*sizeof(whatever_the_structure_is_called) break.
So some of the pbm filters on the freeware CD work, some are self-consistent
(you can exchange files between the Alpha pbm filters) but are inconsistent
with other (e.g., Ultrix) implementations, and some just don't work.  I only
checked out the few that I needed for a particular project, so I can't give
the status of all of them.  The ones that were broken took a significant
effort to fix, though, because the use of types is somewhat sloppy...


