I'm guessing that you are missing the file locore.o (/usr/sys/BINARY/locore.o or /usr/sys/BINARY.rt/locore.o - the latter is for Real Time kernels).  There
is supposed to be a link from /usr/sys/KECK/locore.o to one of the other 
locore.o files.

Somehow, you appear to have lost this file.

This file is part of the OSFHWBIN or OSFRTHWBIN subsets.  You can try to reload
them.  However, the easiest thing would be to grab this file from another V2.0
system.

Good luck,
Dave


