Here's the reply from Rudy:

I understand your frustration with the multiple compilers and debuggers from
Digital on OSF/1 as we update the technology that we provide on our systems.  
This is a temporary situation and at the moment we are half way through the 
migration (in this case from dbx to DECladebug). Ensuring the robustness and 
quality is an essential success factor for this migration. (Which is why we 
are erring on the side of redundancy and confusion.)

When the next OSF/1 release ships this Fall - DECladebug will have all
the functionality of dbx along with many advanced features like stronger
language support, more thread debugging functionality, remote debugging...


Back to me:

The DECladebug team has been working very hard to address as many of the 
quality, robustness, and performance issues as we can.  We've spent many
man years of effort to make the upcoming releases be as good as we can make
them.  

