I got tcsh to work after a bit of hacking, but the 
way it configures seems not very safe to me, so I
finally decided to switch to the gnu bash which 
seems to be supported rather well. 
It installed without _any_ hacking on SunOS, IRIX 
and DEC OSF1.
Like tcsh, it  has the main feature I expect 
from a shell - human useable  command line editing 
(via GNU readline). 
It has ~- expansion, csh job control, tcsh 
filename expansion and POSIX conformance.

It seems to be available from any ftp site which
has the GNU stuff.

