Stephen Morris (mors@tessella.co.uk) wrote:
> I'm having a problem setting up anonymous FTP on a DEC Alpha system running
> OSF/1 V2.0.

> I've set up user anonymous in /usr/ftp, and created the subdirectories pub, bin
> (containing ls), etc (containing truncated passwd and group files), and sia
> (containing copies of all the DEC SIA files).  When I connect to the anonymous
> FTP account, the "ls" command works successfully, but "ls -l" fails:

	1. copy /sbin/loader onto /usr/ftp/sbin/loader
	2. copy /usr/shlib/libc.so onto /usr/ftp/usr/shlib/libc.so

	If you intend to run wu-ftpd , add the necessary binaries for 
	on-the-fly conversions (GNU tar, gzip, compress, gztoZ) onto
	/usr/ftp/bin or onto /usr/ftp/sbin and add the shared libraries
	they need onto /usr/ftp/usr/shlib ( 'odump -Dl executable' to see
	what they need).
	Then copy your local time zone from /etc/zoneinfo onto /ftp/etc/zoneinfo
	in order to get the right local time zone in welcome banner. E.g.,

36 [12:36] gilles@myhost:/ftp> ls -l /ftp/etc/zoneinfo
-rw-r--r--   1 root     anonftp      588 Jun  6 10:11 MET
lrwxrwxrwx   1 root     anonftp        3 Jun  6 10:13 localtime -> MET

