There is software, but no manual. The video functions are accessed via
the XV X server extension. The headers are in

	/usr/include/X11/extensions/Xv*

the library is accessed via

		-lXv

> Now there is a group
>here that has the DECstation/Ultrix version of the DECvideo/PIP board, and
>it comes with a software package called DECmedia, which DECdirect assures
>me is not needed/does not exist for AXP OSF/1.

The XV pieces of XMedia and OSF/1 are identical. You can use their manual
pages and examples to get you going. If you want more sample programs and
documentation, get the sources from

	gatekeeper.dec.com:pub/X11-contrib/xv2r2.tar.Z

which contains quite a few.

