I've been using three ST12550N disks for about 6 months with no problems!

You don't need to add a disktab entry if they are data disks, just
use the disklabel command with a type of 'rzxx'.  OSF will query
the drive for its size and give you one large C partition with the
whole drive in it.  works great!

 /sbin/disklabel -w [-r] [-n] disk disktype [packid] [primary-boot
  secondary-boot]
 
ie:  /sbin/disklabel -w -r rz4 rzxx

would label the disk on scsi id 4.

Good luck!

Dave
