If you give disklabel a name that isn't the disktab file,
it will ask the disk driver for the size, partitioning and
geometry.  Once the disk label has the information newfs
doesn't need it:

	# disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c st1255on
	# newfs /dev/rrz#c

The feature doesn't have any way to get the rotational
speed, so you may want to edit the label to set it to
the correct value.
