Another thing to try is gtar (gnu tar). It uses the rsh stuff transparently
so that you can:

	gtar cvf nother::/dev/rmt0h

Note: the gnu tar package calls itself tar, not gtar. I installed it as
gtar to prevent confusion on my part as to what I was really running.

Note: on earlier OSF/1 releases /etc/rmt is not present (used by gtar
for remote operations):
	ln -s /usr/sbin/rmt /etc/rmt
solves that problem.

