I had a little bit of a problem building it, but, i DO have
binaries, if you are interested in that.

were your problems linking either:

* decnet objects still in the libc? (old osf 1.2/early 1.3 problem if
  you don't have decnet)

* you need _eprintf.o

* you don't have libJPEG or libTIFF

my solutions:

for the first one, either build on a machine
with decnet, or compile this program to a .o 
and add it to libc.a


----------begin dnet.c-----------

#include <stdlib.h>

int dnet_conn()
{
  return 0;
}

struct dn_naddr* dnet_addr()
{
  return(NULL);

}

struct nodent* getnodebyname()
{
  return(NULL);
  
}

---------end dnet.c----------

type:

cc -c dnet.c
ar rv /lib/libc.a dnet.o

for the second problem, if you have gcc installed on your
system:

ar xv /.../gcc-lib/alpha.../libgcc.a _eprintf.o

now, edit Makefile, look for main.o and add _eprintf.o to that line.


I personally would recommend building this baby only with cc.

for the last problem, either get and build libjpeg and libtiff,
or comment those parts out of the Makefile and rw/Makefile.


-- craig




