Try tcp_wrapper from ftp.cert.org.  It allows you to limit which machines
have access to services (ftp, telnet, rlogin, shell, etc) on your machine.
You specify this using hosts.allow and hosts.deny files.  It works by replacing
the existing services in your inetd.conf file (you do that) with the wrapper
program.  It in turn calls the appropriate service program once the requestor
machine has passed the verification.

 
