If you are running a version of OSF/1 prior to V2.0 Rev. 250
you might want to upgrade to this rev. There was a bug floating 
around in the early times of V2.0 that could lead to your problem.

If the problem persists (it can be a *real* problem), it means
the file table in your kernel is not big enough. Edit your config
file, raise "maxusers", and rebuild your kernel 
(doconfig -c <MACHINE_NAME>).

Hope this helps,
-Philippe

