Hi,

We are running DEC OSF/1 V1.3A, V1.2 Worksystem Software on our ALPHA boxes
and I seem to have stumbled on a bug in the Korn Shell implementation.

If you begin the PATH= declaration with /bin then the built in 'echo'
command fails to recognise escape sequences yet the built in 'print'
command is fine.


ie:

$ PATH="/usr/bin:/bin"
$ echo "no carriage return \c"                CORRECT BEHAVIOUR
no carriage return $

$ PATH="/bin:/usr/bin"
$ echo "no carriage return \c"                ERRONEOUS BEHAVIOUR
no carriage return \c
$


Yet 'print' works:

$ PATH="/bin:/usr/bin"
$ print "no carriage return \c"
no carriage return $



Anyone else experienced this?

