I believe that you must also remove "LOGNAME" from the environment;
telnet tenaciously tries to use whatever it can find with your name
in it.  I don't know if this can be done or not from .telnetrc

>I, too, find this default behaviour unacceptable.  Especially since it seems
>to surpress the pre-login banner on most systems, and that pre-login banner
>often contains information on how to log in to special guest accounts.
>I like the existence of the feature, but I very much dislike the default.

I don't know about supression of the pre-login banner, but I do agree
that this is annoying, and I filed an internal bug report on the problem
a few weeks ago.  Meanwhile, there's an easy workaround.

Create this shell script:

#!/bin/csh -f
unsetenv USER
unsetenv LOGNAME
/usr/bin/telnet $*

And either call it "telnet" and put it in your search path before
/usr/bin (and before /usr/ucb, which is a link to /usr/bin) ... or
call it something else (for example, "telnet_why_cant_DEC_get_this_right").

-Jeff "Works in research, not in the OSF product group"


